---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { PARTS, OFFERS } from '../../data/services';

// Prices live on one page, one level down, reachable from every service but
// never sitting in front of someone who is still deciding whether the work is
// worth reading about. A buyer looks for the number; everyone else was only
// ever being taxed by it.
---

<Page
  title="what it costs -- alexander campos"
  description="Prices for every system and every way to start. Fixed scope, fixed price, stated in full."
>
  <article class="pricing">
    <h1>What it costs</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Fixed scope, fixed price, agreed before anything starts. If a build turns out
      to be smaller than it looked, the number comes down. Everything below is a
      range because the spread is real, and the <a href="/services/pricing#start">Teardown</a>
      is what turns a range into a number.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>The eight systems</h2>
      <p class="note">Typical build range and timeline. Credited against a larger build if you take one.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>System</th><th>Range</th><th>Timeline</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {PARTS.map((part) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={`/services/${part.slug}`}>{part.name}</a></td>
              <td class="num">${part.priceFrom.toLocaleString()}–${part.priceTo.toLocaleString()}</td>
              <td class="dim">{part.timeline}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section id="start">
      <h2>Ways to start</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Offer</th><th>Price</th><th>Who it's for</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {OFFERS.map((offer) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{offer.name}</td>
              <td class="num">{offer.price}</td>
              <td class="dim">{offer.who}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <p class="close">
      Nothing here is a subscription you have to cancel except Operator, which is
      month to month. <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a> and I will tell you which
      one you actually need, including when it is none of them.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  .pricing { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--white-60); max-width: 62ch; }
  .note { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--white-45); }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 1rem; }
  th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--white-45);
    font-weight: 400;
    padding: 0 0.8rem 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15);
  }
  td { padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem 0.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-08); vertical-align: top; }
  td.num { font-family: var(--mono); white-space: nowrap; color: var(--glow-hot); }
  td.dim { color: var(--white-45); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .close { color: var(--white-60); max-width: 62ch; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    td.dim, th:last-child { display: none; }
  }
</style>
